{"id": "EUVD-2026-82058", "enisaUuid": "1e848ac3-84bf-39f6-a314-f3895d83cfd5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfirmware: qcom: scm: Fix NULL dereference in IRQ handler before __scm is published\n\nIn qcom_scm_probe(), devm_request_threaded_irq() is called before\nsmp_store_release(&__scm, scm). Two paths can dereference __scm before\nit is published, both causing a NULL pointer dereference.\n\nThe IRQ handler receives scm via its data argument but passes only wq_ctx\nto qcom_scm_waitq_wakeup() and qcom_scm_get_completion(), which then\ndereference __scm directly. Thread scm through both functions so the IRQ\nhandler path never touches __scm.\n\nNon-atomic SMC calls made during probe (e.g. from qcom_tzmem_init via\nqcom_scm_shm_bridge_enable) can return WAITQ_SLEEP, causing\nqcom_scm_wait_for_wq_completion() to run before __scm is published and\ndereference it. Add platform_set_drvdata(pdev, scm) early in probe and\nchange qcom_scm_wait_for_wq_completion() to take the device pointer and\nuse dev_get_drvdata() to reach scm, removing any dependency on __scm.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9c1e3da0a206270e5df470ca1c82de52190d68c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b451f38cb7f5bca78484362347f039c08c94de95", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d753df5899ec356272d08bc4718e82844e4bdf0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f312ef5026678f14caf1378c5f7fffdf667f9c81", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/966d23c7e68ea32679275a7e3d2383181002c868"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gcqw-f4ff-hx84", "CVE-2026-90397"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07c5e4c2-b16a-33a8-a6cc-134842487759", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6bf32599223634294cdc6efb359ffaab1d68073c <f312ef5026678f14caf1378c5f7fffdf667f9c81"}, {"id": "0c632d3b-d3bb-3547-bf3c-14d5aa6b6534", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "12180d31-68fa-3ef9-a585-84458ead9f65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "127ca1b0-74f4-33e6-9620-1fa6f4a1bedc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6bf32599223634294cdc6efb359ffaab1d68073c <966d23c7e68ea32679275a7e3d2383181002c868"}, {"id": "501c10de-46f2-3078-95f9-b7f8e9cf9a5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6bf32599223634294cdc6efb359ffaab1d68073c <b451f38cb7f5bca78484362347f039c08c94de95"}, {"id": "600d6546-c506-3c0e-b393-3c1e54cb3aa9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.3"}, {"id": "60e3e050-756d-3150-89e0-86283f0b8229", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6bf32599223634294cdc6efb359ffaab1d68073c <1d753df5899ec356272d08bc4718e82844e4bdf0"}, {"id": "6e607e5c-789b-3612-9bbe-403672ac6877", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8ad9cd7b-1bc9-3b72-a1a3-5c1703d61873", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "aad957da-7bad-39aa-ba70-d917b83b2781", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6bf32599223634294cdc6efb359ffaab1d68073c <c9c1e3da0a206270e5df470ca1c82de52190d68c"}, {"id": "d9e35d39-4c7d-36c6-b626-54fc4194b5c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "ddeb65a0-c057-383c-b66d-94889f0cf9c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "89b35f0c-5e7d-31eb-83cc-27dca2350a14", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}